504 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1342 0 R
/E (Our benchmarking shows that no single scene graph generation model performs best across every metric and dataset.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
505 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1343 0 R
/E (REACT demonstrates strong relationship recall, while REACT++ provides a promising balance between prediction performance and inference speed. Fast Contextual SGG also shows competitive relationship prediction on PSG.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
506 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1344 0 R
/E (Based on these findings, we have provisionally selected REACT++ for further development. However, our ultimate objective is not just scene graph generation; it is reliable object retrieval in dynamic workspaces.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
507 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1345 0 R
/E (Our next step is to validate the models on workspace-specific data, address occlusion and changing relationships, and integrate scene graphs with memory for more reliable object retrieval.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
